    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm putting together a hypertrophy-focused program for a client. Can you give me a technical breakdown of how Leucine specifically interacts with the mTOR pathway to trigger protein synthesis? Also, I need a quick explanation of how a caloric surplus impacts nitrogen balance in this context. Thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Leucine acts as a direct anabolic signaling molecule, binding to and activating the Rag GTPases, which subsequently activates mTORC1. This activation initiates the phosphorylation cascade that drives the translational machinery to synthesize new muscle protein. A caloric surplus ensures you have sufficient energy substrates (calories) and amino acid availability to support this enhanced protein synthesis. By providing excess energy, the surplus shifts the body toward a positive nitrogen balance, meaning net protein accretion exceeds protein breakdown.",
      "source": "target",
