    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Got it, thanks. One more thing—I've been reading some conflicting stuff about how cellular processes like this aren't always linear and can be influenced by \"micro-disruptions\" in the metabolic environment. From a physiological standpoint, what are the main factors that could potentially interfere with or dampen that mTOR signaling cascade even if the leucine threshold is met?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Several factors can dampen mTOR signaling even with adequate leucine intake. High levels of systemic inflammation or insulin resistance can impair the sensitivity of signaling pathways upstream of mTOR. Furthermore, chronic energy deficit or inadequate sleep severely stresses the body, shifting it into a catabolic state that suppresses anabolic signaling. Finally, certain nutrients or stressors, like excessive chronic cortisol exposure, can exert direct inhibitory effects on mTOR activity.",
      "source": "target",
